/**
 * ============================================================================
 * HUB - CHEMICALS: sanitation chemical and supply ordering (shown on screen as the Ordering hub)
 * ============================================================================
 * Version 0.9: the Log tab, the chemical clerk's quick log that replaces the paper day sheets. Jugs, barrel changes and
 * returns in a few taps (the chemicals and amounts used most on top, How many for several jugs), titrations with the
 * target shown and the reading marked in or out of range (drops or PPM; an out-of-range reading asks what was done), and
 * the day's entries below with Same again, Again and Fix. An entry not yet seen in Dataverse stays on this device and is
 * checked by its own id, so a press never saves twice. The clerk view opens on Log.
 * Version 0.8.2: Chemical use says more about the old log. The week tiles go by the last whole week logged and say how
 * far the log is written; titration readings with no target show their most common reading (and flag one that hardly
 * ever changes); rows with no MSS area are named (barrel changes, room-only spellings like Creme side); Where it goes by
 * weekday (with gallons per day); an estimated cost per week and month; and highlights under the tiles.
 * Version 0.8.1: no browser pop-ups, which Power Apps blocks without a word. Close as received and Cancel cart ask on the
 * page (Yes / No under the buttons), and a copy the browser refuses shows the text on the page to copy by hand.
 * Version 0.8: the page is called the Ordering hub on screen. Insight has a Chemical use view, read from the chemical usage
 * log (gallons issued by week and month, where it goes by chemical, room, area, shift or application, titration checks in
 * and out of range, an estimated cost), next to Spend and stock. A View switch at the top (Admin: every tab; Chemical
 * clerk: Insight on Chemical use, Import, Lists), kept on this device; Dataverse security roles still decide who can
 * save. White space under the last row, so the bottom of a tab scrolls clear of the app's edge.
 * Version 0.7: the Count tab, a blank inventory: every stock row in walk order with an empty box to fill in on screen or
 * on the printed sheet, saved as that day's counts and as stock on hand. Typed counts stay on this device until saved.
 * Version 0.6: the Insight tab (spend by month and by week, where the money goes by item, category or distributor, bought
 * versus used between counts, and stock against the minimum). It only reads; every chart has a Show as table view.
 * Version 0.5: old chemical log day sheets on the Import tab (a sheet with its form header, several sheets, or a month of
 * the prepared file in one paste; each row is saved under its sheet day and its place on the sheet), a panel for names the
 * hub does not know (picks saved to the _c_ Chemical alias table), and the Chemical names list on the Lists tab.
 * Version 0.4: the Lists tab (area spellings of the old chemical log with their MSS area, spot and room, and the titration
 * targets, edited in place), and suggested carts packed 5% under the cart limit because SAP prices can differ.
 * Version 0.3: the Import tab. Paste from Excel (a Week sheet, the cart Log sheet, the INDEX sheet, or any import file);
 * rows are matched to Dataverse by key, previewed as new / update / no change / problem, and written on Import.
 * Version 0.2 (phase A): the Ordering tab. Suggested carts per distributor under the cart limit (from stock, open carts,
 * weekly use worked out from the Sunday counts, and requests), paste-ready text for SAP, the cart tracker (draft, submitted,
 * approved, ordered, received), clerk requests, and alerts (quotes, prices, vendors, carts left open).
 * Version 0.1 (phase 0): the Tables tab. Every Dataverse table this hub will use, with its display and logical names, the
 * data type of every column, whether the hub needs it, and a Dataverse check that reads the TABLE DEFINITIONS (never rows,
 * apart from one tiny count per table) and says what is found, missing, typed differently or not readable.
 * Later phases add the Sunday count, the clerk checklist and more insight views (plan:
 * chemical-ordering-plan.md in the project folder).
 *
 * Same look as Manager Hub v6.6 (company blue / yellow / red, Tailwind from https://cdn.tailwindcss.com loaded by the page).
 * Host rule: the host compiles to ES5 with no iterable support. Only arrays, plain objects, index loops, forEach / map and
 * Promises are used: no for-of, no Set or Map, no spreading anything but arrays.
 * Writes happen only on a button press: in the Ordering tab (save a draft cart, move a cart on, receive, add a request),
 * in the Count tab (Save count, Save walk order),
 * in the Log tab (Log, Same again, Save titration, Try again, Save changes),
 * in the Import tab (Import) and in the Lists tab (Save).
 * The Insight and Tables tabs only read.
 *
 * DATAVERSE MAPPING CHEAT SHEET (owned by this hub; read-only tables from other apps are listed in CH_SPEC too)
 * | craa5__c_distributor       | Distributors (Ecolab, Grainger, Vincit, Star Steel ...)                       |
 * | craa5__c_chemical          | Chemical list (item master): every chemical, test reagent, supply and PPE item that is ordered  |
 * | craa5__c_chemicalinventory | Stock now, per item and storage location                                       |
 * | craa5__c_cart              | One SAP shopping cart (header)                                                 |
 * | craa5__c_cartline          | One item on a cart, or a request waiting for the next cart                     |
 * | craa5__c_chemicalcount     | One item counted on the Sunday count                                           |
 * | craa5__c_chemicalusagelog  | Chemical log: jugs issued, point-of-use barrel changes, returns, titrations    |
 * | craa5__c_titrationtarget   | PPM target range per chemical and application                                  |
 * | craa5__c_checklisttask     | The chemical clerk checklist tasks (editable)                                  |
 * | craa5__c_clerkchecklist    | One shift's completed checklist                                                |
 * | craa5__c_chemicalstandard  | Expected chemical use per clean (links MSS cleans to chemical cost)            |
 * | craa5__c_areaalias         | Old area spellings mapped to MSS areas                                         |
 * | craa5__c_sanitationbudget  | Monthly sanitation budget (later)                                              |
 * ============================================================================
 */

