                        {!targetRows.length && !adds.some(function (a) { return a.list === 'target'; }) && <p className="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-slate-600" data-lst-empty="target">{G.error ? 'The titration targets could not be read, so none are shown. Press Refresh to read them again.' : 'No titration targets yet. Press Add target for each chemical and application on your target list.'}</p>}
                    </div>
                </div>}
            </div>}
            {ready && view === 'names' && <div className="mt-6">
                <h2 className="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#00468B]">Chemical names</h2>
                <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">Names the Week sheets and the chemical log use for a chemical that Chemicals does not have by that name: a typo (Syergex), a catalog number (56918 Quat 10X Titrate -042), an old name. Each name points at one item, so its rows import under that item. Leave the chemical blank to leave the name out for now: its rows are skipped with a note. Names that differ only in capitals or spaces count as one. The Import tab adds a name here when you pick it there.</p>
                {N.missing ? <p className="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-[#FFB81C] bg-[#FFF6E0] px-3 py-2 text-sm text-[#7A4B00]" data-lst-missing="names">Dataverse has no _c_ Chemical alias table yet. Create it from the prompts file in the chemical-ordering folder, then press Refresh.</p> : <div>
